drills.statement:
Split text into words on any whitespace (spaces, tabs, newlines - possibly several in a row),
lowercase every word, and return a map word -> number of occurrences. Ignore empty strings.

Example: "the cat The  dog" -> {the=2, cat=1, dog=1}

Return a map from word length -> list of the words with that length, keeping the words
in the same order they appear in the input.

Example: [hi, cat, yo, dog] -> {2=[hi, yo], 3=[cat, dog]}

nums is NOT sorted. Exactly one pair of different indices i < j has nums[i] + nums[j] == target.
Return {i, j} with i < j. Must be O(n) - the last test has 200,000 numbers.

Example: [2, 7, 11, 15], target 9 -> {0, 1}

a is sorted ascending and has exactly one pair of different indices i < j with
a[i] + a[j] == target. Return {i, j}. Use two pointers (O(n), O(1) extra space).

Example: [1, 2, 4, 7, 11], target 9 -> {1, 3}
